# One of the images on hraj.si and in the README, regenerated per release by
# tools/make-screenshot.sh rather than captured by hand. The page's previous set
# was six years old and two of them showed a menu bar that no longer exists.
#
# The camera and the shader are pinned in the matching *-user.json, passed with
# --user-settings, so the shot cannot drift with the session and the real
# user.json is never touched.
#
# Under a stereo shader. Everything on the board is drawn twice, once per eye,
# each pass tested against its own depth — which is why the annotations do not
# clip along a stone's silhouette. Needs red/cyan glasses to fuse, and the
# caption on the page has to say so or it reads as a rendering fault.
load_sgf res/screenshot/hero-13x13.sgf
wait_idle
navigate_start
wait_idle
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
navigate_forward
wait_idle
expect view_position 47
expect stereo true

toggle_coordinates on
toggle_next_move_overlay
# The anaglyph mode comes from stereo-user.json, not from the `anaglyph` command:
# the command reports what it did into #lblMessage, and that caption then sits
# across the middle of the picture.
expect anaglyph gray

toggle_fullscreen
wait 1500
screenshot res/screenshot/stereo.ppm
